# ============================================================
# Cross-machine consistency policy (machineB) — SCOPED
# TRACK : only .py / .md that belong to the comparison + mae_anomaly
#         experiments (their code + runner scripts + docs).
# IGNORE: everything else (all other dirs, binaries, data, json, .txt,
#         notebooks, caches, results, deprecated/legacy, .claude, CLAUDE.md).
# ============================================================

# 1) ignore everything, but keep descending into directories
*
!*/

# 2) whitelist .py / .md ONLY inside the experiment areas ----
!comparison/**/*.py
!comparison/**/*.md
!mae_anomaly/**/*.py
!mae_anomaly/**/*.md
!scripts/**/*.py
!scripts/**/*.md
!docs/**/*.py
!docs/**/*.md

# 3) experiment-related root docs + keep .gitignore ----------
!/README.md
!/ablation_guideline.md
!/set_guideline.md
!.gitignore

# 4) re-exclude — WIN over the whitelist above ---------------
# results / deprecated / caches inside the tracked areas
comparison/results/
comparison/_deprecated/
**/_deprecated/
**/__pycache__/
docs/report_images/
# .py junk
*_backup*.py
*_option*.py
*.bak

# 5) hard-exclude non-experiment dir trees entirely (root-anchored).
#    Wins over `!*/`; also blocks embedded git repos / edge cases under them.
/temp/
/.trash/
/trash/
/dataset/
/legacy/
/references/
/ResearchProposal/
/.claude/
/configs/
/results/
